## 📊 Complexity Analysis

| Algorithm | Time Complexity | Space Complexity |
|------------|----------------|------------------|
| Minimax | O(bᵈ) | O(d) |
| Alpha-Beta Pruning | O(bᵈ) Worst Case | O(d) |
| Alpha-Beta Pruning | O(bᵈ⁄²) Best Case | O(d) |
| Heuristic Alpha-Beta | O(bᵏ) | O(k) |
| MCTS | O(N × Simulation Length) | O(N) |

Where:

- **b** = Branching Factor
- **d** = Search Depth
- **k** = Depth Limit
- **N** = Number of Simulations

---

## 📈 Results

The implementation successfully demonstrates:

✅ Optimal move generation using Minimax

✅ Reduced search effort using Alpha-Beta Pruning

✅ Faster decision making using Heuristic Alpha-Beta

✅ Simulation-based move selection using MCTS

---

## 🎯 Conclusion

This project demonstrates four important Artificial Intelligence search algorithms and compares their behavior in a Tic-Tac-Toe environment.

The implementation validates the correctness of:

- Minimax Search
- Alpha-Beta Pruning
- Heuristic Alpha-Beta Search
- Monte Carlo Tree Search (MCTS)

while highlighting the trade-offs between optimality, efficiency, and scalability.
